{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he was incensed.</b> I have already explained this matter: the burnt offering and the meal offering prolong anger against the wicked. Dathan and Abiram were great men and they had offered a meal offering before this deed. This is the meaning of “Do not turn to their offering,” and turn to me, “for I have not lifted [even] one donkey of theirs.”" "And the meaning of נשאתי is: I placed a burden upon it." "<b>nor have I done harm.</b> In any matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:59.535797685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}